## Staking System Overview

The system allows users to stake tokens and earn rewards in USDC and ADX. In `resolve_staking_round`, the staking rounds that are completed and have their rewards calculated are stored in `resolved_rounds`. 

There is a maximum limit on how many resolved rounds may be stored. When this limit is reached, the oldest resolved round is removed. When the oldest resolved staking round is removed, the USDC rewards associated with this round are effectively redirected to the current staking round, ensuring they are still available for distribution.

```rust
> _public/staking/p/resolve_staking_round.rs
pub fn resolve_staking_round(ctx: Context<ResolveStakingRound>) -> Result<()> {
    [...]
    // Remove round from accounting
    {
        let oldest_round = staking.resolved_staking_rounds[oldest_staking_round_index];
        let stake_token_eligible_to_rewards =
            oldest_round.total_stake - oldest_round.total_claim;
        let unclaimed_rewards = math::checked_decimal_mul(
            oldest_round.rate,
            -(Cortex::RATE_DECIMALS as i32),
            stake_token_eligible_to_rewards,
            -(staking.staked_token_decimals as i32),
            -(staking.reward_token_decimals as i32),
        )?;
        staking.resolved_reward_token_amount -= unclaimed_rewards;
        staking.resolved_staked_token_amount -= stake_token_eligible_to_rewards;
    }
    [...]
}
```

However, ADX rewards do not have the same redirection mechanism. Instead, they remain locked in the `staking_lm_rewards_vault` and are not redistributed to the current round. As a result, these rewards become inaccessible to users, resulting in a situation where staked ADX rewards are effectively lost.

## Remediation
Calculate and redirect the unclaimed ADX rewards similar to the USDC rewards when removing the oldest resolved staking round.

