## Infrared Vault Registration and BGT Emissions

## Context
Infrared.sol#L241-L250

## Description
When a vault (InfraredVault) is registered for a corresponding asset, the asset's gauge (BerachainRewardsVault) is never checked to determine whether it is a "friend of the chef." In Berachain, BGT tokens are emitted only for gauges that are registered in BeraChef (`chef.isFriendOfTheChef(gauge)`). If a vault is registered for an asset that is not eligible for BGT emissions, users might inadvertently stake in this vault without earning any rewards, and vote for it without the vote being able to count.

## Impact
The impact is low as no funds are lost; however, users might stake tokens without earning rewards or vote for vaults that cannot be included in the final cutting board distribution.

## Likelihood
The likelihood is low as Infrared's Keeper contract will likely not create vaults that are not eligible for BGT rewards.

## Recommendation
Document and make it clear to users that Infrared vaults might not be eligible for any BGT rewards. Alternatively, check whether a staking asset's gauge is a "friend of the chef" when creating the rewards vault.

